{{Information
|Description={{en|1=The '''Coat of arms of Liverpool City Council''', the local government authority for the City of Liverpool in Merseyside, England. The blazon is:<br>'''''ARMS:''' Argent a Cormorant in the beak a Branch of Seaweed called Laver all proper.''<br>
'''''CREST:''' On a Wreath of the Colours a Cor­morant the wings elevated in the beak a Branch of Laver proper.''<br>
'''''SUPPORTERS:''' On the dexter Neptune with his Sea-Green Mantle flowing the waist wreathed with Laver on his head an Eastern Crown Gold in the right hand his Trident Sable the left supporting a Banner of the Arms of Liverpool on the sinister a Triton wreathed as the dexter and blowing his Shell the right hand supporting a Banner thereon a Ship under sail in perspective all proper the Banner Staves Or.''}}
|Source=*[[:File:Wildman_Supporter_(Heraldry).svg|Wildman_Supporter_(Heraldry).svg]]
